{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following MS C++ code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original MS C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include<cstdio>\n#include<cstdlib>\n#include<fstream>\n#include<queue>\n#include<stack>\n#include<cstring>\n#include<algorithm>\n#include<vector>\n#include<list>\n#include<set>\n#include<string>\n#include<map>\n#include<cmath>\n#include<iostream>\n#include<ctime>\nusing namespace std;\ntypedef long long ll;\ntypedef long double ld;\n\nll gcd(ll x, ll y) {\n    while (y != 0) {\n        ll t = y;\n        y = x % y;\n        x = t;\n    }\n    return x;\n}\n\nll lcm(ll x, ll y) {\n    return x / gcd(x, y) * y;\n}\n\nld diff(ll x1, ll y1, ll x2, ll y2) {\n    ll common = lcm(y1, y2);\n    ll num1 = common / y1 * x1;\n    ll num2 = common / y2 * x2;\n    return ld(abs(num1 - num2)) / ld(common);\n}\n\nint main() {\n#ifndef ONLINE_JUDGE\n    freopen(\"input.txt\", \"r\", stdin);\n    freopen(\"output.txt\", \"w\", stdout);\n#endif\n    ll x, y, n;\n    cin >> x >> y >> n;\n    ll best_num = 0, best_den = 1;\n    ld target = ld(x) / ld(y);\n    \n    for (ll i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        ll lo = 1, hi = 1000000;\n        while (lo + 1 < hi) {\n            ll mid = (lo + hi) / 2;\n            ld val = ld(mid) / ld(i);\n            if (val < target) lo = mid;\n            else hi = mid;\n        }\n        ll candidate = (diff(lo, i, x, y) > diff(hi, i, x, y)) ? hi : lo;\n        if (diff(candidate, i, x, y) < diff(best_num, best_den, x, y)) {\n            best_num = candidate;\n            best_den = i;\n        }\n    }\n    cout << best_num << \"/\" << best_den;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static long gcd(long x, long y) {\n        while (y != 0) {\n            long t = y;\n            y = x % y;\n            x = t;\n        }\n        return x;\n    }\n\n    static long lcm(long x, long y) {\n        return x / gcd(x, y) * y;\n    }\n\n    static double diff(long x1, long y1, long x2, long y2) {\n        long common = lcm(y1, y2);\n        long num1 = common / y1 * x1;\n        long num2 = common / y2 * x2;\n        return Math.abs(num1 - num2) / (double) common;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long x = sc.nextLong();\n        long y = sc.nextLong();\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        \n        long best_num = 0, best_den = 1;\n        double target = (double) x / (double) y;\n        \n        for (long i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n            long lo = 1, hi = 1000000;\n            while (lo + 1 < hi) {\n                long mid = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                double val = (double) mid / (double) i;\n                if (val < target) lo = mid;\n                else hi = mid;\n            }\n            long candidate = (diff(lo, i, x, y) > diff(hi, i, x, y)) ? hi : lo;\n            if (diff(candidate, i, x, y) < diff(best_num, best_den, x, y)) {\n                best_num = candidate;\n                best_den = i;\n            }\n        }\n    